# Swan Compiler 2 — Linker Driver
#
# Link emitted object files and required runtime/library inputs into the final
# executable, shared library, or WebAssembly artifact.
#
# Responsibilities:
# - Select the linker/toolchain compatible with the target triple.
# - Pass explicit object, library, search-path, and entry-point arguments.
# - Preserve argument boundaries; never build shell command strings.
# - Capture exit status and diagnostics from the external linker.
# - Support compile-only output without invoking a linker.
# - Reject unavailable cross-link toolchains with an actionable diagnostic.
#
# The linker is the final build stage. It does not parse Swan or optimize SVM.
#
# Implementation status: contract; port the process and toolchain behavior
# from Compiler 1 linker.h after object emission is available.
